Analyzing the demo: the 7s form a diagonal line that was extended through background cells until it hit the edge, while the 3-line was blocked by a non-background cell (2) and the 7-line's other direction was blocked by 0s. So the rule: extend each same-color diagonal line in both directions, filling only background cells, stopping at edges or non-background cells.

In the test, the 3-line at (3,3),(4,2) heads down-left but is blocked by 4 at (5,1); extending up-right through background gives (2,4), (1,5), (0,6) = 3. The 7-line at (3,0),(4,1) is blocked both ways, so unchanged.

